“From my first day, the House system made me feel part of a family. I’ve made lots of friends, enjoy fun clubs like baking and homework club, and my teachers support me every step of the way. I’m proud to be part of HAWI.”
“My teachers make lessons really interesting and their passion makes me want to learn more. I love history. The trips we go on, especially our residential to Chester, make learning fun and bring us closer together.”
“HAWI has helped me discover my passions and grow in confidence. Finding my love for drumming inspired me to choose Music GCSE, and the incredible support from my teachers has helped me become more resilient and confident.”
“Being part of the team has shown me the importance of encouragement, teamwork, and believing in one another.”
“I strongly believe that this is a school that any ambitious and motivated student would thrive in. I am incredibly grateful to have experienced all that I have in my two years here.”
@harriswimbledon • Oct 1
This week, we’re shining a spotlight on Year 9 Enrichment, where students have been getting creative, learning new skills and trying something different! There’s been plenty going on across the school, including potting plants in Gardening, making jewellery boxes, and learning new drills at CCF. Enrichment gives students the chance to step outside the usual classroom setting, discover new interests and develop practical skills — all while having fun along the way! #Enrichment #Afterschool #Year9 #Creative
@harriswimbledon • Sep 30
The Hockey team came back for the first week of their club in fun fashion - we had a great time reminding ourselves how to play and had an exciting game on top. We have 15+ regular players in Year 10 who are the backbone of the hockey club; most of them joined in Year 7 and 8! Since then, they've medalled in both Open London competitions and state school championships. We are encouraging all lower years to come and join this friendly, competitive and fun club. #Hockey#Team#Training#Teamwork#hawi
@harriswimbledon • Sep 30
Congratulations, Santhosh! 🎉 Congratulations to Santhosh, Y13, who has been named a Prize Winner in the KS5 Poetry category of the 2026 Young Writers’ Competition! @wimbookfest A fantastic achievement and a wonderful recognition of his creativity and talent in poetry. ✨ Well done, Santhosh! 👏 #YoungWritersCompetition #Poetry #CreativeWriting
@harriswimbledon • Sep 30
Our Year 9 students enjoyed a special talk at New Wimbledon Theatre celebrating the graphic novel adaptation of Lord of the Flies. They heard from illustrator Aimée de Jongh, Judy Golding, William Golding’s daughter, and Joel Wilson, Executive Producer of the BBC adaptation. Our students asked thoughtful questions and even had their copies signed by Aimée! ✍️📖 A memorable experience for all! 🌟 @wimbookfest #LordOfTheFlies #Year9 #Literature #GraphicNovels
@harriswimbledon • Sep 30
Last Friday, we came together to raise money for the Macmillan Coffee Morning! 💚 A huge thank you to everyone who baked, donated cakes or sent money in to support this very worthwhile charity. We were overwhelmed by the incredible number of cakes brought in by our students — hundreds in total! 🎂🧁🍪 Points were awarded for the number of cakes, with additional points for homemade bakes and outstanding efforts. Thank you to everyone who helped make the morning such a fantastic success! 💚 #MacmillanCoffeeMorning #Macmillan #BakeSale #Fundraising
@harriswimbledon • Sep 25
Wishing our Year 11 students an amazing time as they embark on their Silver DofE practice expedition! 🥾⛰️ We hope you have a fantastic experience, challenge yourselves, support one another and make some great memories along the way. Good luck, Year 11! 🌟 #DofE#expedition#teamwork#challenge#HAWI
